    <string name="info_title">Info &amp; rules</string>
    <string name="info_about_title">About the app</string>
    <string name="info_about_text">A score keeper for the tile game Qwirkle: manage players, record rounds, and view results and statistics.</string>
    <string name="info_privacy_title">Your data</string>
    <string name="info_privacy_text">All data stays on this device. The app sends nothing over the internet and needs no account. Use \"Back up &amp; restore\" to create a backup file and restore it later.</string>
    <string name="info_rules_title">Rules (short version)</string>
    <string name="info_rules_intro">Qwirkle is played with tiles in six colors and six shapes. Each player holds six tiles and takes turns adding to the tiles already on the table.</string>
    <string name="info_rules_turn_title">A turn</string>
    <string name="info_rules_turn_text">You place one or more tiles in a straight line. Every line that results must share either one color or one shape, and no tile may appear twice in a line. Then you draw new tiles. Instead of placing, you may swap tiles.</string>
    <string name="info_rules_points_title">Points</string>
    <string name="info_rules_points_text">For every line your move touches, you score one point per tile in that line, including tiles already placed. A tile that belongs to two lines counts in both. Completing a line of six tiles is a Qwirkle: it earns 6 bonus points on top.</string>
    <string name="info_rules_end_title">End of the game</string>
    <string name="info_rules_end_text">The game ends when the bag is empty and a player has placed all of their tiles. That player gets 6 bonus points. The player with the most points wins.</string>
    <string name="info_rules_app_title">In this app</string>
    <string name="info_rules_app_text">In each round, enter the points without the Qwirkle bonus and count the Qwirkles. The app adds 6 points per Qwirkle itself. You choose the end bonus of 6 points when finishing. The game is meant for 2 to 4 players; the app allows up to 7. See the game instructions for the exact rules.</string>
    <string name="info_rules_disclaimer">This is an independent score keeper and is not affiliated with the rights holders of Qwirkle.</string>
    <string name="info_licenses_title">Licenses</string>
    <string name="info_licenses_text">The app uses Android Jetpack (Compose, Room, Navigation, Lifecycle) and Material Design. These libraries are licensed under the Apache License 2.0.</string>
